\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces RAVEN-MCS aligns asynchronous federated completion with a public deployment target. (a)~Three selection layers induce an arrival law that need not match the deployment target. (b)~RAVEN-Design forms a selection-corrected target-mass reference and calibrates it in the current feasible support. RAVEN-NoDesign uses $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \zeta $}\mathaccent "0362{\zeta }=1$ and is not target-mass reconstruction. The Design setting is fixed before the window opens and held throughout it; the coverage Gate is a separate diagnostic. (P2) is the per-window calibration program that maps this reference onto the feasible aggregation set; it is defined in Section~\ref {sec:calibration}.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
